Package/part text had separate finite AST and linker adapters but no atomic path into the selected model. This importer composes those real prerequisites with one owned model transaction: create all declarations, resolve forward/qualified local references through explicit AST-to-JSON-node bindings, then stage typing for a single caller commit. Cancelled, malformed, unresolved, stale, foreign or colliding work cannot publish a partial import.

The finite family is named packages, part definitions and usages. Explicit caller NodeIds preserve semantic/resource identity. Existing model typing retains its semantic-ID string encoding; native bare-reference interchange remains excluded. Current Java declaredName apostrophe stripping is pinned through the actual importer/attribute call chain, including its escaped-name quirk; AST lookup remains independent of transformed labels.

Validation: thirteen Rust integration tests, formatting, all-target Clippy and eight source pins pass. Tests exercise actual parser/linker/model composition, forward references, selected containment, identity distinctions, quote translation, cancellation and failure/history boundaries. The original 10-pass/three-failed fixture capture and corrected passing capture retain exact executed sources, runners, streams and unchanged-input hashes. Independent parent source review found no blocking issue within the finite scope. No native Syside/Java importer or complete SysML interchange is claimed. This PR follows F13, which contains the exact F11 prerequisite; land prerequisites, retarget and revalidate. Held graph/factory paths and shared manifests remain unchanged.
